# SABOTAGE: A7 (ADR-047 §10a row 19 / R-A6-3, THE F-4 LOCK) gate sabotage — a tool re-enters
# the loop. `Samen.Automation.Actions.FetchRecord` exports `tool_schema/0` (it IS an
# agent-callable tool), and this patch makes it NAME `Samen.AI.Agent.start` — exactly the
# raw-spawn recursion escape the static F-4 lock exists to refuse. `mix samen.verify.agent_coverage`
# scans every app's lib/ by AST and MUST flag any `tool_schema/0` module that calls
# `Samen.AI.Agent.start/run`, so its coverage floor over the real tree goes RED. This is the
# single most load-bearing A7 assertion: a future edit cannot silently reopen the escape.
# The positive control (a clean tool that does NOT re-enter stays green) proves it non-vacuous.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_coverage_verifier_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: violations/1 is empty on the real umbrella tree
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/actions/fetch_record.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/actions/fetch_record.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/actions/fetch_record.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/actions/fetch_record.ex
@@ -72,6 +72,12 @@ defmodule Samen.Automation.Actions.FetchRecord do
   @impl true
   def effect, do: :read
 
+  # SABOTAGE (ADR-047 A7 / F-4): a `tool_schema/0`-exporting module (an agent-callable
+  # tool) NAMES the loop-entry primitive `Samen.AI.Agent.start` — reopening the raw-spawn
+  # recursion escape the static F-4 lock forbids. `mix samen.verify.agent_coverage` MUST go
+  # red (a tool may never re-enter the loop, regardless of which spawn primitive it reaches).
+  def __f4_reentry_backdoor__(ctx), do: Samen.AI.Agent.start(__MODULE__, ctx, "recurse", [])
+
   @impl true
